Rain pattered against the tall library windows, tracing silvery rivers down the fogged glass. The scent of wet earth mingled with the musty perfume of old pages, while yellow lamplight warmed the heavy shadows between shelves. Readers nestled in corners, listening to the soft drumming from above, their fingers gliding quietly over spines and words. Each turn of a fragile page felt like a small rebellion against the world outside—a world washed in grey, alive only in reflection.